& [IntentionAndFindings]
  + read existing packaging rather than presume a new bundle duplicates no prior work
  + historical provider-free bundle contains four different binaries and binds codex/self-hosted-corpus published HEAD current lock and target/release paths; its authority does not silently import into this integration branch or the new inspection executables
  + existing deterministic store-ZIP fixed timestamp exact allowlist rederived manifest nonextracting verifier and mutation tests provide useful design patterns only
  + installed llvm-readobj read-only PE import inspection on the intermediate focused-release MCP binary observes Windows system API and VCRUNTIME140/UCRT prerequisites; no DLLs copied installed or downloaded
  + intermediate focused-release MCP executable3877888 bytes SHA2564B6EEB212C662F4D531F7B06E97B9440C6D61E15A7D0CEF22B91947FB5AA3E9D and stdio1289728 bytes SHA2567F7E721D3CF6E05BC85042986E65DE988CA29EF913FEB685B5BE16376CDD5DA9 show a small capability seed is feasible
  + those intermediate bytes may change with later build-feature unification; any package must rebuild and remeasure selected exact inputs after publication rather than reuse these as frozen release identity
  + valid semantic seed SOP must use the actual kind/context/term language rather than mislabel a narrative-format SOP file as executable kernel grammar

& [PotentialSuccessor]
  + after MCP closure source-preserve and separately sign a Windows inspection-runtime seed containing only the two bounded executables exact semantic seed SOP golden/request fixture operator guide and closed package manifest
  + metadata and recipe may enter Git while developer ZIP/runtime copies remain small outside Git in a fresh scoped D build-output child; no new bulky target
  + a new producer should have no replacement or recursive-cleanup option and use create-new absent-target publication so a preflight absence check cannot silently authorize a later overwrite
  + producer and independent archive verifier prove deterministic identity from identical inputs not cross-build binary reproducibility or publisher authenticity
  + bounded developer replay may prove the SOP is interpretable by the existing stdio runtime; no auto-extraction install service launch application configuration provider model remote host or autonomous work

& [ResultAndUnresolvedFrontier]
  + read-only research complete no package source contract signature implementation extraction or execution performed
  + current MCP full workspace debug/release Clippy evidence attribution and publication remain the first priority
  + potential seed is a narrow semantic-inspection capability handoff not the full self-updating Cantor runtime plus model product
